        boundary: 'These are active Buddhist and Taoist spaces, not abandoned caves. Prayer, ceremonies, residents and posted photography or footwear rules take precedence over a sightseeing route.',
        stages: [['Choose the anchor', 'Confirm whether Sam Poh Tong, Ling Sen Tong or Nam Thean Tong is open to visitors on your date. Ask about ceremony periods, shoes, photography and any restricted interior.'], ['Match the approach', 'Use the official BAS.MY map to inspect the Gunung Rapat and Sam Poh Tong labels, then verify the live route and closest stop. Otherwise book a ride to the named gate.'], ['Visit slowly', 'Keep one temple as the main visit. Read the signs, leave worshippers clear of the threshold and do not touch cave formations or feed resident animals.'], ['Return deliberately', 'Arrange the ride back before entering the compound or confirm the actual bus departure and last connection. Shift to a short Old Town meal if rain or fatigue ends the second visit.']],
